\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces GARCH(1,1) conditional volatility of the domestic gold premium before and after the May 13, 2026 duty hike. Post-hike volatility is 1.48$\times $ the pre-hike level (Levene $F = 11.46$, $p = 0.0008$, though the Levene test rests on only 31 post-hike observations and should be interpreted as indicative). Estimated persistence $\alpha + \beta = 0.990$ is likely upward-biased: fitting GARCH across a level break treats the May 13 premium jump as a large volatility shock, mechanically inflating persistence; re-estimation on break-adjusted residuals would provide a lower bound on true volatility clustering.\relax }}{16}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:garch}{{4}{16}{GARCH(1,1) conditional volatility of the domestic gold premium before and after the May 13, 2026 duty hike. Post-hike volatility is 1.48$\times $ the pre-hike level (Levene $F = 11.46$, $p = 0.0008$, though the Levene test rests on only 31 post-hike observations and should be interpreted as indicative). Estimated persistence $\alpha + \beta = 0.990$ is likely upward-biased: fitting GARCH across a level break treats the May 13 premium jump as a large volatility shock, mechanically inflating persistence; re-estimation on break-adjusted residuals would provide a lower bound on true volatility clustering.\relax }{figure.4}{}}
\citation{KanjilalGhosh2014}
